---
template_name: "mcp-tool"
description: "MCP tool code generation template"
category: "mcp"
variables:
  tool_name: "my_tool"
  description: "A helpful tool"
  return_type: "str"
  async_handler: true
  params: []
---
# MCP Tool: {{ tool_name }}

## Tool Definition

```python
@self.server.tool()
{% if async_handler %}async {% endif %}def {{ tool_name }}(
{% for param in params %}
    {{ param.name }}: {{ param.type }}{% if param.default %} = {{ param.default }}{% endif %},
{% endfor %}
) -> {{ return_type }}:
    """{{ description }}
    
    Args:
{% for param in params %}
        {{ param.name }}: {{ param.description }}
{% endfor %}
    
    Returns:
        {{ return_description | default("Result of the operation") }}
    """
    try:
        # Implementation
{% if implementation %}
        {{ implementation | indent(8) }}
{% else %}
        result = {
            "status": "success",
            "message": "{{ tool_name }} executed"
        }
        return json.dumps(result)
{% endif %}
    except Exception as e:
        return json.dumps({
            "status": "error",
            "error": str(e)
        })
```

## Registration

```python
class MyServer(BaseMCPServer):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__("my-server")
        self.server = FastMCP(self.server_name)
        self.setup_tools()
    
    def setup_tools(self):
        # Tool is registered with @self.server.tool() decorator
        pass
```

## Usage Example

```python
# From MCP client
result = await client.call_tool("{{ tool_name }}", {
{% for param in params %}
    "{{ param.name }}": {{ param.example | default("...") }},
{% endfor %}
})
print(result)
```

## Testing

```python
import pytest
import json

@pytest.mark.asyncio
async def test_{{ tool_name | snakecase }}():
    # Initialize server
    server = MyServer()
    
    # Call tool
    result = await {{ tool_name }}(
{% for param in params %}
        {{ param.name }}={{ param.test_value | default("...") }},
{% endfor %}
    )
    
    # Verify result
    data = json.loads(result)
    assert data["status"] == "success"
```
